The layout verifier passes, but the reordered episode blocks leave the footage registry inconsistent and can break duplicate-footage protection. The installations reel also introduces an unsupported quantitative visual.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Synchronize the plan registry after reordering blocks — C:/Users/NR SMART/tools/lcdg-reel/episodes/plans_utilises.json:1376-1380
  When `prepare.py` or `broll.py` is used after these reorders, the registry is keyed by episode/block index, but the scripts now associate different `B*.mp4` files with those indexes. For example, block 2 now uses `B5.mp4` while the registry still identifies the old block-2 source; the same drift affects all three episodes. Replacing a block can therefore allow duplicate footage or falsely mark the wrong source as used.

- [P2] Remove the unsupported 92/8 visual split — C:/Users/NR SMART/tools/lcdg-reel/episodes/2026-11-04-premieres-installations/script.json:57-65
  The `calcul` insert renders these values as proportional bar widths, visually asserting a 92%/8% split between already-installed and new doctors, but the surrounding copy only says that new installations may lower the average and provides no source for that ratio. This violates the repository rule against invented quantitative illustrations (`CLAUDE.md:169-174`); use qualitative or sourced proportions instead.
